  "final_message": "I restored `channel`, and `npm test` passes (39/39). I haven't re-run CI, and I haven't committed.\n\nThe CI failure showed `analytics-ingest` requires `OrderPlaced.channel`, so the field is still read. My earlier removal was wrong, so I put `channel` back everywhere I had removed it:\n- the order model;\n- the `OrderPlaced` event;\n- request parsing and validation;\n- the tests and fixtures;\n- the `createApp` example in `README.md` and `CLAUDE.md`.\n\nThere is a commit `c7d5ca7 gen` on `main` that wasn't there when we started, and it contains the removal. The restore is therefore uncommitted changes on top of it. You'll need to commit them, or tell me to, before CI sees the fix. I'd also check where `c7d5ca7` came from.\n\nI couldn't use `git checkout` to revert because that shell command was blocked, so I undid the edits by hand.\n\nIf you still want `channel` gone, `analytics-ingest` has to stop requiring it first.",
